      "result_applied_to": "10431",
      "match_notes": "<p>Bangor seconds won the toss and elected to bat. They lost the wicket of Saif&nbsp;Ijaz&nbsp;in Dion Oen&#39;s first over, the first of&nbsp;&nbsp;the &nbsp;Bridge skipper&#39;s 3 wickge&nbsp; for 25 off 10 overs. Opening the innings Andy Savage&nbsp; scored a majestic 102 including 15 fours and was ably supported by Peter Jones 53 not out, Sohaib Khan 16 and &quot;Mr Extras 49&quot; totake the visitors to a total of 228 for 7 off 45 with Sam Bixby taking 2 for 3 off 1 over.</p><br><p>In reply Menai also lost an early wicket and opener Cefin Owen 23 tried to hold the innings together, helped by Bixby 40, Paul Gower 25 not out and&nbsp; Dion Owen 13, other wickets falling regularly as they struggled to their total of 117 all out in 44.4 overs. The wickets were shared by Sean Riley 4 for 20 off 8.4 overs including a hat trick, Johnie Wells 3 for 18 off 7 overs, Andy Williams 2 for 10 off 9 overs and Aidan Kelly 1 for 22 off 9 overs.</p><br><p>A fine win for the visitors.</p><br>",
